{"title":"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are 3 numbers A, B, and C, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e7b77423bbddf9a5787077cf1814a9779925a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001C - 2002A = 4004$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"183\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e559c195df562719b773a903e287446e8f0818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001B + 3003A = 5005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"183\" height=\"14\" />. What is the average of A, B, and C?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32ba813750c886ea9ca372376808a31ff1b1115c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\text{Not uniquely determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"524\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that we don't need to find what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> actually are, just their average. In other words, if we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8ada654c9fa78d44e7304d40dd67f978b80847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B+C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />, we will be done. \n</p><p>Adding up the equations gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd7c9cc30c42e5c28cc82daf4213511f832e95e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001(A+B+C)=9009=1001(9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"284\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e733c66e31ed787f813159f23d83ed0e2e81ddfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B+C=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> and the average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c59cbf771dbe0ac85e85aaa2909519ecfad61e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{3}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4faa3b02b5b2deb20b9cae1911c4231bd3342042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As there are only 2 equations and 3 variables, just set one of the variables to something convenient, like 0. Setting C as 0, we get A is -2, and B is 11 by substitution. By basic arithmetic the average is 3=&gt;B\n</p><p>-dragoon\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start by isolating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in both of the equations, in order to represent the variables <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of A. Ending up with the two equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/26028f68fc607a2db45f1d1b5e0f9c2a17e61d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 2A +4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d4ddefea219613890b9e19092a38a656321a782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = -3A + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />, we have to calculate the value of the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d086dade7a8f0e1d121c0f2db930086be6c78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A+B+C}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6e4a2ad19fddde8f1ddc900d6ec191ef4bf2f50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/0533d5ba2bd421186c7976c63f09b5df985879c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3A + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, we add them up and end up with a value of 9. Dividing 9 by 3 to compute the average, we get our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4faa3b02b5b2deb20b9cae1911c4231bd3342042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Darth_Cadet\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take the first equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e7b77423bbddf9a5787077cf1814a9779925a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001C - 2002A = 4004$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"183\" height=\"13\" />. Notice that there is a common factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888c508062c09735bab7ff0e11e7dc80cc7580db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so take it out to create the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc013458246920e129910b5b344aab529fdc4964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001(C - 2A) = 4004$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />. Divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888c508062c09735bab7ff0e11e7dc80cc7580db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d29e0d1a7a7c4ffba281dc18f55670938e45a990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-2A = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. Take the next equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d29c0b623017ae090c0e0b000f26192aeb4ea0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001B+3003A = 5005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"16\" />. Once again, notice that there is a common factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888c508062c09735bab7ff0e11e7dc80cc7580db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so factor it out to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/3303cb2282944b76429d962fab692662cf3fd5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001(B+3A) = 5005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />. Divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888c508062c09735bab7ff0e11e7dc80cc7580db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> on both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce6174bf10f2297d3b262ed3e189be0ccc8c640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B+3A = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />. Because we need the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d086dade7a8f0e1d121c0f2db930086be6c78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A+B+C}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />, combine the two newly found equations using variables to attain that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5649bb5b076efa6cbafe21a71dc43bdbd14fdef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(C-2A) + (B+3A) = A + B + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"283\" height=\"20\" />. Substitute the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ce34505b60a57420d2704b5b129a501ce25fa66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B + C = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />. Finally, divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get the average, getting the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4faa3b02b5b2deb20b9cae1911c4231bd3342042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>-N.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0k8f5Y5ciSU\">https://youtu.be/0k8f5Y5ciSU</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A\">2002 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195947\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 302/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2322/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7160/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.835      1 -total\n 61.31%    7.869      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 37.69%    4.838      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7470:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195947 and revision id 280661. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}